DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261010
SUMMARY:Deadline: NetHope: Humanitarian AI Research Fellowship 2026 (Remote
 )
DESCRIPTION:NetHope\, the consortium of more than 60 humanitarian\, develop
 ment and conservation organizations working with over 70 technology compan
 ies\, is piloting a short-term Humanitarian AI Research Fellowship to grow
  the pool of researchers and practitioners who understand how AI can respo
 nsibly advance humanitarian work\, producing findings its member organizat
 ions can put to immediate practical use. Two parallel streams: Stream 1\, 
 AI Adoption and Governance (case studies of how humanitarian and nonprofit
  organizations adopt\, govern and manage risk around AI tools\; suited to 
 backgrounds in policy\, program evaluation or humanitarian systems) and St
 ream 2\, AI Systems and Localization (evaluating open-source and open-weig
 ht models for humanitarian use\, local versus proprietary systems\, low-co
 nnectivity deployment\, fine-tuning prompt and dataset libraries\; suited 
 to computer science\, machine learning or applied data science backgrounds
 \, with model evaluation or red-teaming experience a plus). ELIGIBILITY: m
 id-career to seasoned practitioners with strong writing and analytical ski
 lls\, internationally open\; fellows must pass an OFAC screening. NetHope 
 owns all research outputs and IP\; fellows are credited as named authors. 
 HOW TO APPLY: CV\, letter of interest answering three set questions\, 2-3 
 references\, optional writing sample\, via NetHope's online form. NetHope 
 may review applications and select fellows before the closing date\, so ap
 ply early. DEADLINE: 9 October 2026.\n\nOrganisation: NetHope\nLocation: R
 emote\, internationally open.\nAward: Stipend\; the amount is not publishe
 d in the call (details are shared with selected fellows and set out in the
  fellowship agreement). Part-time\, approximately 10 hours per week. 4 to 
 6 fellows selected. No application fee.\nDuration: Mid-November 2026 throu
 gh February 2027\, part-time (approx. 10 hours per week).\n\nMore: https:/
 /nethope.app.box.com/f/0377bdadf36e4b74b2f244fe07cd9f9b?utm_source=artific
