SUMMARY:Deadline: Saul Kagan Fellowship in Advanced Shoah Studies 2027-28 (
 PhD and Postdoc)
DESCRIPTION:Flagship fellowship strengthening Holocaust studies and Shoah m
 emory worldwide\, open to PhD candidates and postdoctoral researchers from
  around the world for the September 2027 to August 2028 academic year. Eli
 gible disciplines include history\, anthropology\, cultural studies\, Jewi
 sh studies\, political science\, philosophy\, religion\, sociology and wom
 en's studies. TERMS: up to USD 30\,000 per academic year\, renewable once\
 ; no residency requirement beyond attending and presenting at the annual w
 eek-long summer workshop\, so fellows work from their home institution. CO
